 34P  c  1977Na05: 34Si was produced via the 18O(18O,2p)34Si reaction with the  
 34P 2c  32-MeV 18Q{+5+} beam from one of the Brookhaven National Laboratory MP 
 34P 3c  tandem Van de Graaffs. Targets were Ta2O5 enriched to 99% in 18O. |g   
 34P 4c  rays were detected using a coaxial Ge(Li) detector. |b particles were  
 34P 5c  detected using a NE102 plastic scintillator. Measured E|b, E|g, I|g,   
 34P 6c  and |b|g coin. Deduced levels, decay branching ratios, log {Ift},      
 34P 7c  parent {+34}Si T{-1/2} and masses.                                     
